<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Chitradurga Nayakas</h1><p class="st-meta">1588 CE – 1779 CE (approx.) · capital Chitradurga</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Poligar chiefs who ruled the fortress of Chitradurga in Karnataka, remembered for the legend of Onake Obavva.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayakas</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chitradurga">Chitradurga</a> were Beda chiefs who served the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> as local military governors. After Vijayanagara's defeat in 1565 they gained autonomy, and by the 1580s they ruled from the hill fortress of Chitradurga, whose seven concentric walls were extended by successive rulers.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayakas</a>, also called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palayakkarar">Palegars</a>, ruled a dry upland territory of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> through warrior clans and revenue from farming and herding. They made shifting alliances with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/keladi-nayaka-kingdom">Keladi Nayaka kingdom</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mysore-1399-1799">Kingdom of Mysore</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madakari-nayaka-v">Madakari Nayaka V</a>, the last ruler, is a folk hero in Karnataka.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mysore-1399-1799">Kingdom of Mysore</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chitradurga">Chitradurga</a>, and the fort fell in 1779 after a long resistance; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madakari-nayaka-v">Madakari Nayaka</a> died in captivity. Legend says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onake-obavva">Onake Obavva</a>, a guard's wife, killed many attackers with a pestle in an earlier siege.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/chitradurga-nayakas.jpg" alt="Chitradurga Nayakas" width="320" height="452"><figcaption>Image: H. SHASHIDHAR of the Indian Administrative Service and N. SREENIVASA MURTHY Geographer of the DCD, Karnataka DIRECTOR... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Showing_territories_of_Nayakas_of_Chitradurga_Kingdom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1588 CE – 1779 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chitradurga</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Madakari Nayaka V</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kannada</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nayakas of Chitradurga, Palegars of Chitradurga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1684&amp;focus=chitradurga-nayakas" aria-label="Chitradurga Nayakas on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6771 1648 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chitradurga Nayakas lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7091 1904L7107 1971"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7107 1971h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7091 1904h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7091 1904h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Chitradurga. <a href="/atlas?year=1684&amp;focus=chitradurga-nayakas">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

